@BeforeSuite is used for one-time global setup like reports.
@BeforeTest runs before a test block in testng.xml for environment setup.
@BeforeClass runs once per class for common setup like browser launch.
@BeforeMethod runs before every test case when we need fresh setup.”

When to use @BeforeSuite -
Use it for things that should happen only once:
Initialize Extent Reports
Load config.properties
Start Selenium Grid
Set global variables
Connect to DB (once)

When to use @BeforeTest -
Use it when setup should run per test group:
Set environment (QA / UAT / PROD)
Set API base URI
Browser selection (Chrome / Firefox)
Initialize test data for that test block

